From b28e40387eb1245926eb17cb332288fe5ac6514d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:05:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] redact: a query's value ends at its & (#5074)

A URL that hands its key over in the query carries the next
parameters after it, and & is one of the characters a value may
have: api_key=demo_key_ABC123456789&page=2&page_size=20&sort=desc
went out with page, page_size and sort inside the placeholder, the
next parameters' names and values for the vendor to read where the
key's value ends. The local model takes its neighbours the same
way: sess=AbCdEf123456&page=2 found as one value, the page
parameter went with it.

inURLQuery says the value at s[a:] is a query's field's: the =
before it ends a name, and walking back over the names and the =,
&, ., - and : between the fields, a ? or an & stands before the
first of them. A value of prose, or a quoted one, walks into a
space or a quote first and keeps its own & as it did (password:
ab&cd12345). An & a value carries url-encoded is %26, no & at all.

queryValueEnd is where such a value ends: at the & that starts the
next parameter. The three SECRET rules that take a value after a
field's name cut theirs there (queryValueAt, in place of
secretValue), and fieldAt takes a value in a query for its field's
whatever words it is made of: demo_key_ABC123456789 reads as a
name in code, and there it is the key's value. The model's span is
cut the same way.

Run (this tree): go test ./internal/redact -count=1: ok. go test
./internal/gateway -run 'Redacted|PlaceholderNote|MaskedRequest'
-count=1: ok. gofmt -l internal/redact: clean. go vet
./internal/redact ./internal/gateway .: clean. go build .
./internal/redact ./internal/gateway: ok.
Red before the fix: TestMask red on all four query cases (&page=2
&page_size=20&sort=desc sent inside the placeholder),
TestModelQueryValueEndsAtAmpersand red (&page=2 went with the
value).
Not tried: the real local masking model (the tests use the
stand-in model the suite's other model finds use), a real query
key against a real vendor.

